  "id": "perceived-competence",
  "term": "perceived competence",
  "definition": "Perceived competence is a person’s sense of how capable they are at a task. In learning, it can shape how they respond to negative feedback, with higher perceived competence linked to more adaptive coping, especially when the task is also interesting.",
